\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mi>z</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mo>\u00b1</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mo>\u00b1</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>.</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n<p>Since the tangent of this angle can be a positive or negative number, the <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"226\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D467 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>-coordinate can also be positive or negative.</p>\n<p>On the other hand, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"227\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D703 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>\u03b8</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> can vary arbitrarily in its domain. </p>\n<p>Therefore, our surface is the cone shown below.</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-104236-e-0\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-104236-e-0\"></div> </div></div>",
